{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And they will eat and be sated and grow fat and turn to other elohim.</b> This indicates that the passage is concluded with the First Temple, for there — they ate and drank, and they served foreign worship, and there they served the Baalim; and this is what it says: <b>and they will serve them and spurn Me and break My covenant.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The Hebrew contains parenthetical glosses of apparent corrected readings: '(שמנו עשתו)' corrected to '[שבענו ושתו]' (they ate and drank), and '(עברו דברי רע)' corrected to '[עבדו עבודה זרה]' (they served foreign worship). Translated the corrected readings. The verse fragment 'ועבדום ונאצוני והפר את בריתי' appears to continue the citation from the same passage (Deuteronomy 31:20)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:45.638297897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}